Suppress outbound activity-status notifications.

Make Api::SendProgressManager::send() a no-op so the client never sends
messages.setTyping actions: typing, recording, uploads, sticker/location/
contact selection, game play and group-call speaking.

Read receipts, online status, message content and receiving-side
behaviour are intentionally unchanged.

diff --git a/Telegram/SourceFiles/api/api_send_progress.cpp b/Telegram/SourceFiles/api/api_send_progress.cpp
--- a/Telegram/SourceFiles/api/api_send_progress.cpp
+++ b/Telegram/SourceFiles/api/api_send_progress.cpp
@@ -109,6 +109,8 @@
 }

 void SendProgressManager::send(const Key &key, int progress) {
+	// Patched: never broadcast local activity status to the peer.
+	return;
 	if (skipRequest(key)) {
 		return;
 	}
